  "limitations": [
    "One direct same-job checkout.ok boolean equality consumer followed by one checkout child; no generic DATA continuity, task parameter transfer or whole-result record.",
    "Normal native git completion establishes boolean true. Failure propagates before the binding and consumer; no false result record or recovery is invented.",
    "Only literal branch checkouts with full history are admitted; no revision-SHA, shallow, nested, cross-job, path output or persistent/mutable state claim.",
    "The observer reads native checkout arguments, error origins and workspace markers independently of generated source and mutant identity. Groovy local values are not directly inspected; the bound artifact and consumer behavior establish the limited evidence.",
    "The unchanged compiler-generated Jenkinsfile executes on an isolated controller without external egress or published ports. Runtime hosts and observation transport remain trusted.",
    "This fills one bounded value/state observation row. It does not promote generic support, portable execution or milestone closure."
  ]
